<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <!-- The Ed25519 expanded secret key lives only in caller-supplied scratch memory and is handed
         to the crypto P/Invokes as a raw pointer: reading MemoryHandle.Pointer (a void*) after
         pinning to obtain that nint requires unsafe context. -->
    <AllowUnsafeBlocks>true</AllowUnsafeBlocks>
    <Description>The libsodium crypto binding for the Lumoin family: Ed25519 seed-keypair generation, detached signing and verification, Ed25519-to-X25519 key conversion, X25519 scalar multiplication, XChaCha20-Poly1305 authenticated encryption, and the ML-KEM-768 (FIPS 203) and X-Wing hybrid post-quantum KEMs as thin Span-based LibraryImport wrappers. Secret-key scratch memory is composed by the caller as a MemoryPool&lt;byte&gt; (guarded native, locked, pinned or managed backing), so the binding depends only on Lumoin.Base, carries no native assets and is identical on every target. The libsodium native library resolves at runtime on desktop and server targets and is statically linked at publish on browser-wasm.</Description>
    <PackageTags>libsodium;sodium;ed25519;x25519;curve25519;signing;verification;key-conversion;xchacha20poly1305;aead;ml-kem;x-wing;post-quantum;lumoin</PackageTags>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- Directory.Build.props adds SupportedPlatform browser to every non-Tests project. Unlike
       Lumoin.Base.Sodium and Lumoin.Base.MemoryProtection, whose memory-protection P/Invokes cannot
       exist in a browser, this binding KEEPS the browser platform on purpose: the same LibraryImport
       bindings are satisfied on browser-wasm by statically linking a family-built libsodium.a into
       dotnet.wasm at publish (NativeFileReference in the consuming app), and guarded scratch simply
       is not composed there — the caller picks a managed or pinned pool instead. -->

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="../Lumoin.Base/Lumoin.Base.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Lumoin.Base.Libsodium.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
